{
  "schemaVersion": "lifeline.power-network.v1",
  "networkId": "cigre-mv-der-v1",
  "provenance": {
    "source": "CIGRE Task Force C6.04.02, Benchmark Systems for Network Integration of Renewable and Distributed Energy Resources, CIGRE Technical Brochure 575 (2014): European medium-voltage benchmark network",
    "implementation": "pandapower.networks.create_cigre_network_mv(with_der='all'), pandapower 3.2.2 (BSD-3-Clause)",
    "builtNetworkSha256": "f742f489c1e9f9b56ef7fb9ffd9420288b85d5120e06ae72bd7af0cc7fa15f28",
    "builtNetworkHashMethod": "sha256 of canonical JSON of bus/line/trafo/switch/load/sgen/storage/ext_grid tables (pandas orient=split, 15 digits)",
    "assumptions": [
      "Essential designations are scenario assumptions: CI3 emergency operations centre, CI7 water pumping station, CI9 hospital.",
      "Battery energy capacities are not given by the benchmark builder; 4-hour duration at rated power and 50% initial energy are scenario assumptions. Builder charging set-points are replaced by an explicit zero command.",
      "Voltage band 0.90-1.10 pu and 100% thermal loading are scenario engineering limits, not equipment ratings; the unfaulted benchmark operates near 0.945 pu.",
      "The 120 s tie-closure delay stands in for fault location and manual switching; it is not a measured utility response time."
    ]
  },
